 Also additive in 6.6: `detectors[].excluded_by_depth`: the explicitly requested `--depth` whose projection cleared a fact the detector requires, when that is the only reason it did not run (`null` otherwise). Each such detector stays listed with `not_evaluated: true` and its `coverage_gap` (now `<fact> not available at depth <d>`, without the duplicated `disabled:` prefix); `coverage_warnings` carries one `Detectors not applicable at --depth <d>: ...` summary line instead of one line per detector. That line is requested scope, not an evidence gap: it is not a PR-comment limitation and lowers neither `confidence` nor `analysis_assurance`. Additive, so a MINOR bump. Never affects `verdict`, `severity` or any exit code.
